FOLLOWUP (out of AC scope, iOS driver): ui_errors_ios has the SAME class of defect.
- no validity channel: empty output at a dead/unbooted simulator reads as clean (no exit 2, no 'scanned N')
- selector omits AppLogger [FAIL]/[ERR] and 'Another exception was thrown'
- bare 'not found' (Android tightened this to '" not found' to avoid matching [WARN] msg="... not found")

# ui_errors_ios [seconds]  -> stream the Runner process log briefly and surface
# Flutter/Dart error signatures (empty = clean). Default 6s window.
# Catches the GetX red-screen, type-cast crashes, widget exceptions, overflows.
ui_errors_ios() {
  local secs="${1:-6}"
  xcrun simctl spawn booted log stream --style compact \
      --predicate 'process == "Runner"' --timeout "${secs}s" 2>/dev/null \
    | grep -aiE "FlutterError|EXCEPTION CAUGHT|is not a subtype|not found|overflowed by|Get\.(put|lazyPut)|Unhandled"
}
